rerun: this replaces two earlier attempts of this log, neither committed. The first, sha256 61cbe7faf59d1d9917d67e5ef466215a88c87795a5e97896a5af385c0227dd50, invoked the gate as "$(pwd)/scripts/check.sh" inside a subshell that had already cd'd to /, so the command was not found (exit 127), and discarded the stderr that would have named the cause. The second, sha256 0e132c350251e14523e1e14acfc32cfbda46cba9228060970fbb4fe5f09ff9db, was built from an inline block and so printed no script at all: its four scan numbers had no printed command form and no positive control, while the report cited them, and it ran only five of the eight --only steps although the report claimed --only i686 had been exercised. Independent check 1 found both. This log is a file, prints itself, runs all eight steps, controls every counting form it uses, and is produced at the phase commit 0a337fb after H3 and K3 were restored on planning's ruling.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: no
